WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.568
-The Supreme Court issued
a historic ruling

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:05.538
on LGBTQ civil rights
as officials across the country

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.073
move toward police reform.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.008
Meanwhile,
the president is defending

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.444
the way he walked down a ramp.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.946
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:17.750 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.585
Let's just get this
out of the way first.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.088
The president, as we all know,
is a weird man --

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.623
deeply weird.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.991
And on Saturday, he once again

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.593
showed off
his fundamental weirdness

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.328
after a speech at West Point

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.729
when he slowly descended
a ramp like an old man

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:33.132
being walked across the street
by a boy scout.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.334
You know, for a guy
who constantly

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.535
talks about how tough he is,

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.371
he sure walks like a baby deer
on a frozen pond.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.705
What is wrong with him?

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:41.407
Are we going to have to get him
an Acorn stairlift?

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.708
[ As Trump ] Acorn One.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.276
[ Normal voice ] I watched that,
and for the first time

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:47.079
thought [bleep]
maybe he does have bone spurs.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.415
Naturally, this prompted
a lot of speculation

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:50.617
about the president's health.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.685
Have his bones been hollowed out

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.054
by years of artificial sweetener
and asbestos?

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.790
Is his blood mostly ketchup
and Diet Coke?

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.825
Still, we,
we are not going to speculate.

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:02.862
But if Donald Trump saw
someone else walking like that,

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.764
you know he would definitely
speculate.

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:08.367
He'd be on Twitter all day
saying things like,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.870
"An extremely credible source
tells me the president

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.005
has hamburger leg.
Must investigate!"

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.274
And, yet, Trump couldn't help
but spend time responding

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:16.609
to the speculation on Twitter

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.445
with a truly ludicrous
explanation.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:22.014
-The president tweeted,
"The ramp that I descended

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:25.084
after my West Point commencement
speech was very long and steep,

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.020
had no handrail,
and most importantly,

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.421
was very slippery.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:32.191
The last thing I was going to do
is 'fall' for the fake news

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:33.359
to have fun with.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.462
Final ten feet I ran
down to level ground.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.965
Momentum!"

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.434
-Wow. So liberals, young people,
and women hate you,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.103
and now we have to add
ramp designers to the list.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.638
Okay.
So let me get this straight.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.141
The ramp was long, steep,
and slippery.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.508
It was a Slip 'N Slide.

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:51.777
You're saying the West Point
ramp was a Slip 'N Slide.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.245
[ As Trump ] It was
a very treacherous ramp

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:56.049
coated with oil,
littered with banana peels.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.883
And due to a luggage mix-up,

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:01.120
the only footwear available
to me were a pair of Heelys.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.522
Heelys. You've got to be careful
on your Heelys.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:04.857
[ Normal voice ] So that's
what the president

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.926
chose to spend his time
focusing on this weekend.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.460
Now, generally speaking,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.130
good news has been
hard to come by these days.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.499
So when the Republican-dominated
Supreme Court

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.501
handed down a landmark decision
this morning

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.437
on whether
federal civil rights law

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.773
prohibits discrimination
against LGBTQ people,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.442
I was ready for disappointment.
Then this happened.

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.544
-A major civil rights decision

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:27.480
out of the United States
Supreme Court.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.383 line:0%
The Supreme Court has ruled
that LGBT Americans

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:35.021 line:0%
are protected
by the anti-discrimination laws

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.323 line:0%
of this country
at their workplaces.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:41.727 line:0%
This is a major civil rights
opinion in the Supreme Court.

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:45.030 line:0%
It was written by Justice
Neil Gorsuch

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.733 line:0%
and joined
by Chief Justice John Roberts.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.969
-The decision now is clear
from the Supreme Court.

00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:52.605
They have issued a ruling

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.908
that now bans discrimination
by employers

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.977
against transgender individuals

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.879
and gay individuals.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.782
This is a key, a landmark ruling

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.784
for gay and transgender
individuals.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:08.054
It was actually authored
by conservative justice

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.122
Neil Gorsuch.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.457
He was joined
by the Chief Justice,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.026
John Roberts, as well as
the liberal justices here.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:18.297
It is a massive victory for
transgender and gay individuals.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:21.133
-What?!
Something good happened?!

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.002
This is -- This is incredible!

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.804
Break out the champagne!
What?

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.238
Oh, we don't have any champagne?

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.708
What about wine?
We drank all the wine?

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.977
Is there anything,
anything we could --

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:34.614
That's it? That's literally
the only thing we have?

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.682
Okay.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.649
Break out the canned tuna,
everybody,

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:39.552
because it's time to celebrate!
That's right.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.221
The Supreme Court ruled
that federal civil rights law

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.090
forbids discrimination against
gay and transgender Americans.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.459
It's incredible news.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.460
And it's especially great
because the one thing

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.563
Trump could say,
he had delivered

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.098
for his extremist base
was the Supreme Court.

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:55.134
And now even the Supreme Court
is bucking him.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.135
When Trump heard the news,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.004
he probably needed
a glass of water,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.473
if only he could get it
up to his mouth.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.674
Dude, what's up?

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.543
This is like watching
one of those improv games

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.744
where a performer puts
their arms through some else's.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:08.714 line:0%
This whole time, has it been
President Trump and Ryan Stiles?

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.483 line:0%
Ryan Stiles! Attic reference!

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.017
Can't do that in the studio.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:14.353
Can someone just get Trump
a really long straw

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.955
so we never have to see this
again?

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.657
So, this was a thrilling

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:20.426
and momentous ruling
and comes just days after

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.227
the Trump administration
announced that it was

00:04:22.227 --> 00:04:25.198
rolling back Obama-era
civil right protections

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.933
for transgender Americans
in healthcare.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.301
Because any time
Trump has an opportunity

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:31.504
to be an [bleep] he takes it.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.173
I'd say the Trump presidency
is like a slippery slope

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.442
toward authoritarianism,
but given how bad he is at it,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.010
it's more like a slippery ramp.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.779
Not the last ramp reference,
by the way.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.147
I'd love to tell you it was,
but we are going to circle back

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:43.650
and call it back one more time.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.151
Do you want to try
and see it coming?

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.485
Maybe you can see it coming.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:49.222
So, there was good news today
on LGBTQ civil rights.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:52.891
And at the same time, we're also
seeing a flurry of legislation

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:56.562
and a massive shift in public
opinion on systemic racism

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.264
and police brutality

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.566
amid the historic
Black Lives Matter protests

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:01.667
sweeping the nation.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.836
Thanks to the unprecedented
outpouring

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.371
of public pressure in the form
of mass demonstrations,

00:05:06.371 --> 00:05:08.908
officials across the country
have been moving toward

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.144
police reform in ways
big and small.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.678
The Minneapolis City Council

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:14.680
passed a resolution
to disband the police

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.049
and invest in community-based
public safety programs.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:19.919
The governor of Iowa signed
a police reform bill

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.554
that was passed in one day.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:24.790
The Louisville Metro Council
banned no-knock warrants.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.392
New York State repealed the law

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.661
that kept police brutality
records secret.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.364
Confederate statues across
the country have been toppled.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.633
And cities and states are
barring police

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.334
from using choke holds
and tear gas.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.803
Now, there's
a wide spectrum there.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:39.472
Some of the these moves
are good first steps,

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.140
others are clearly insufficient.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.110
But I have to
say, in the year 2020,

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.212
banning choke holds
and taking down monuments

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:49.382
to white supremacy should be
the absolute bare minimum.

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.983
We shouldn't be satisfied
with that.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.419
It's like going in for a checkup
and your doctor saying,

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:57.322
"Just so you know,
I graduated high school."

00:05:57.322 --> 00:05:59.459 line:0%
People have been pouring into
the streets for weeks,

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:02.228 line:0%
demanding far-reaching changes
and a fundamental rethinking

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:05.464 line:0%
of how much policing we really
need, and what, if anything,

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.766 line:0%
we need policing for,
which is why

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:09.902
the "de-fund police" movement
has gained steam.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.738
In New York City, for example,
the city council has proposed

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:16.609
a plan that would cut $1 billion
from the NYPD budget

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.911
that could be put to use
elsewhere, like in housing,

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.447
healthcare, homeless and mental
health services,

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.682
or de-lousing
the Times Square Elmo.

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:25.684
We might need another billion.

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:28.287
Or how about we spend that money
on a study to find out

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.188
what the hell those liquid
nitrogen tanks

00:06:30.188 --> 00:06:32.091
are doing on the street corners
in Manhattan?

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.592
I mean, I've lived in this city
for two decades.

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:36.261
I have no idea, no idea
what those things are for.

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:38.530
They look like a bonus item
you'd unlock

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.932
in "Grand Theft Auto."

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.434
The more people hear about
the reality of policing

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:45.237
in this country, the more
they agree that small reforms

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:46.739
at the margins are not enough.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:49.709
We need to de-fund and scale
back policing altogether.

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:53.211
For example, here's an insane
headline from 2014

00:06:53.211 --> 00:06:55.047
that resurfaced recently.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.617
"L.A. schools police
will return grenade launchers

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.818
but keep rifles,
armored vehicle."

00:06:59.818 --> 00:07:01.954
Oh, good, I'm glad they returned
the grenade launchers.

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.923
Also, why the [bleep] did they
have grenade launchers?

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:06.192
Were they providing backup
to the hall monitors?

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.861
"We have a student roaming the
hall with no bathroom pass!

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.996
I repeat, no bathroom pass!"

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:12.999
Throughout this crisis,
Americans have witnessed

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.334
police abuse their authority
with impunity,

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:19.004
and sometimes in the most absurd
and inexplicable ways,

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:22.174
as Illinois Congressman
Bobby Rush discovered recently.

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:24.443
-Last week, the Congressman
got word that his office

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:26.178
in Chicago had been burglarized.

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:28.380
But when he went to look
at the surveillance tape,

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.916 line:0%
this is what he found --

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:32.551 line:0%
A group of up to 13
police officers

00:07:32.551 --> 00:07:34.620 line:0%
helping themselves to coffee,
making popcorn,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.354 line:0%
even napping in his office,

00:07:36.354 --> 00:07:39.191 line:0%
while outside stores were being
damaged and robbed.

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:41.894 line:0%
-That's right.
Police officers broke into

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.063 line:0%
a congressman's office to make
coffee and popcorn

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:47.332 line:0%
and take naps without checking
for cameras first!

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:50.169
Did you think bulletproof vests
make you invisible?

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.403
"I don't know what happened,
Sarge.

00:07:51.403 --> 00:07:52.438
I was wearing the vest."

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.206
They treated a congressman's
office

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:57.042
the way George Costanza
treated his desk.

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:59.879
And then there's this truly
insane story from Ohio,

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.114
where police tried to claim
protesters were showing up

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.917
to demonstrations with weapons
until the truth came out.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.453
Columbus Police posted about
a protest bus

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:10.789
being equipped with riot gear --
clubs, rocks, axes, et cetera.

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:13.659
It turns out the bus belonged
to "hippie circus" performers.

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:15.294
The clubs were juggling clubs.

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:18.063
The rocks were crystals
and fossils.

00:08:18.063 --> 00:08:20.566
On the long list
of most threatening people,

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.435
the very bottom entry
is "people who travel

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.269
with crystals and fossils."

00:08:24.269 --> 00:08:25.905
If you're walking down
a dark alley

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:27.306
and you run into a guy
with a crystal,

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:28.574
the only thing you're at risk of

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.609
is a slightly longer
conversation about crystals

00:08:30.609 --> 00:08:32.010
than you probably want to have.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.479
The only other thing worse
than considering that a threat

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:36.849
would be issuing a warning
that a receiving gang of thugs

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:38.517
is catching people's dreams.

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:40.552
"If you hear wind chimes, run!"

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:41.754
I mean, what else do they do,

00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:43.356
pull over a clown car
and conduct a search?

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:44.790
"All right, everybody,
step out of the car.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.125
Yes, you too, sir,
and you and you.

00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:49.494
And that's got to be everybody.
Okay, you too?

00:08:49.494 --> 00:08:51.430
And you and you and you --

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.498
I'm going to need some backup.

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.467
We got, yeah,
more than you think."

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:56.535
So, people have witnessed
firsthand brutality

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.070
and abuses of power
by the police.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.605
And in response,
they're pouring into the streets

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.540
for mass demonstrations
across the country.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.276
It's an unprecedented movement
that has galvanized

00:09:04.276 --> 00:09:05.978
and swayed public opinion,

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:09.415
in which the president still
clearly does not understand.

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:10.983
-What do you think
the protesters --

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:12.785
Not the looters and the rioters.

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:14.787
We're intelligent enough
to know the difference

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:16.422
in our country, right?
-Sure.

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:18.124 line:0%
What do you think they want?

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:20.559 line:0%
What do you think they need
right now from you?

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:23.328 line:0%
-So I think you had protesters
for different reasons.

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:26.899 line:0%
And then you had protesting
also because, you know,

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.034 line:0%
they just didn't know.
I've watched.

00:09:29.034 --> 00:09:31.437 line:0%
I watched it very closely.
Why are you here?

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:32.905 line:0%
And they really weren't able
to say,

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:35.040 line:0%
but they were there
for a reason, perhaps.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.010 line:0%
But a lot of them
really were there

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.611 line:0%
because they're following
the crowd.

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:40.645
-What is wrong with you?

00:09:40.645 --> 00:09:41.914
You think the protesters
were there

00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:43.315
just because they were following
the crowd?

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:45.317
First of all,
this is the age of corona.

00:09:45.317 --> 00:09:46.952
I know you forgot,
but it still is.

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:48.153
Nobody's following a crowd

00:09:48.153 --> 00:09:49.554
without having
a very good reason.

00:09:49.554 --> 00:09:51.524
"You guys gonna walk close
together and chant?

00:09:51.524 --> 00:09:52.924
And, hey, that's
all I need to know."

00:09:52.924 --> 00:09:54.793
Also, what do you mean
some of them were there

00:09:54.793 --> 00:09:56.061
for a reason, perhaps?

00:09:56.061 --> 00:09:59.799
He's so addled, he can't
even say what the reason is.

00:09:59.799 --> 00:10:02.334
He answers questions
about systemic racism

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.536
and police brutality
with all the specificity

00:10:04.536 --> 00:10:06.572
of a mobster who knows his phone
is being tapped.

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:08.440
"I'll meet you down at the place
to talk about the thing,

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:09.841
you know, for a reason."

00:10:09.841 --> 00:10:11.743
Or maybe Trump
was just distracted

00:10:11.743 --> 00:10:14.379
because he knew he had to
go down a ramp in two days.

00:10:14.379 --> 00:10:16.115
[ As Trump ] I'm sorry,
what was the question?

00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:19.451
I was just trying to game
something out in my head.

00:10:19.451 --> 00:10:21.721
We're going to do a careful
step, careful step.

00:10:21.721 --> 00:10:23.522
Okay, maybe a couple
real fast ones.

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:25.591
Yeah, yeah, no, I think --
I think that will look cool

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:27.659
and people will think that was
a cool thing that I did.

00:10:27.659 --> 00:10:29.528
[ Normal voice ] Now,
as we have said before,

00:10:29.528 --> 00:10:30.762
thanks to organizers
and activists

00:10:30.762 --> 00:10:32.131
doing the work on the ground,
in the streets,

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:34.834
we have seen a massive shift
in public opinion in favor

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:36.101
of the Black Lives Matter
movement

00:10:36.101 --> 00:10:38.670
just in a very short period
of time.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:41.640
-Public opinion
appears to be moving rapidly

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.108
in the direction
of the protesters.

00:10:43.108 --> 00:10:45.344
Just look at this graph from
"The New York Times"' "Upshot."

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:47.846
In the past two weeks, support
for Black Lives Matter increased

00:10:47.846 --> 00:10:51.716
by nearly as much as it had
over the previous two years.

00:10:51.716 --> 00:10:54.520
-It was like lightning striking

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.255
when you feel that electricity

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:57.656
building up in a storm.

00:10:57.656 --> 00:11:00.192
-It's true. What we've seen
is a lightning strike.

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:02.428
And Trump has clearly been
struck. I mean, look at him.

00:11:02.428 --> 00:11:04.229
This is why they tell you
to get off the golf course

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:05.897
when you hear thunder.
"Mr. President, what happened?"

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:07.266
[ As Trump ] I don't know,
I was about to play

00:11:07.266 --> 00:11:09.168
a knock-down six iron
into the green,

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:11.403
and the next thing I remember is
waking up in the urgent care.

00:11:11.403 --> 00:11:16.141
Today we saw a historic victory
for LGBTQ civil rights,

00:11:16.141 --> 00:11:18.377
and we're watching
an unprecedented sea change

00:11:18.377 --> 00:11:21.446
in public opinion on systemic
racism in police brutality,

00:11:21.446 --> 00:11:24.850
and the president has decided
he'd rather spend his time

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.318
whining about the media coverage

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:27.586
of the way he walked down
a ramp.

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:30.122
But, clearly,
in the eyes of history,

00:11:30.122 --> 00:11:31.456
Trump is the one slipping,

00:11:31.456 --> 00:11:32.891
while the people fighting
for justice

00:11:32.891 --> 00:11:36.461
are the ones who have the...
-"Momentum!"

00:11:36.461 --> 00:11:38.330
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:41.467 line:0%
♪♪

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:43.269 line:0%
As New York struggles to reopen,

00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:45.204 line:0%
remember that we're still
a city in crisis,

00:11:45.204 --> 00:11:46.939 line:0%
and City Harvest
has been stepping up

00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:48.407 line:0%
to meet the increased need.

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:50.942 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:11:50.942 --> 00:11:53.946 line:0%
Stay safe, wash your hands,
we love you.

